analysis. Among the 36 fetuses without evidence of aneuploidy, six had a poor outcome: two were spontaneous abortions, 
one was a therapeutic abortion of a fetus with hydrops and a pericardial effusion seen on fetopsy; one fetus died at 
birth of pulmonary hypoplasia associated with autosomal recessive polycystic kidney disease, and one fetus each had 
